      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 3.353,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.353,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "we saw how we can retrieve our route parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "and it was working fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "But there are ways to break this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "There are cases where this approach will not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 16.02,
          "en": "and I will show you a typical example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.02,
          "end": 17.94,
          "en": "On our user's component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.94,
          "end": 21.6,
          "en": "we right now always saw that we have the user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.6,
          "end": 24.213,
          "en": "and name we passed on our url.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "Now in here, let me quickly add a router link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 31.83,
          "en": "So I'll add a horizontal line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.83,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "and then add a anchor tag where I remove the ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 38.88,
          "en": "and instead say router link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.88,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "And now I will actually use this syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 47.45,
          "en": "with the squared brackets where I pass an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "and I want to load slash users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "an absolute path to load the correct route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "The second element will be the ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 58.02,
          "en": "So this might be, let's say 10,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.02,
          "end": 60.18,
          "en": "could be a number, could be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.18,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "And then the name, let's say Anna.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "So this will now construct a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 69.69,
          "en": "which is slash users slash 10 slash Anna.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.69,
          "end": 72.36,
          "en": "And this is where this array approach might be better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "because you can really structure this really well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 77.82,
          "en": "and we will soon see how you can even make this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.82,
          "end": 79.053,
          "en": "more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 84.92,
          "en": "So here, I will say load Anna, ID 10, something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "Any text you like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "And now let's see this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "We got this link on our currently loaded page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "with users free Max.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "And if I click this, you see that the URL was updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now it's users 10 Anna, but the text here wasn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.71000000000001,
          "end": 102.50999999999999,
          "en": "And this is not a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.50999999999999,
          "end": 105.50999999999999,
          "en": "This is the default behavior and what is happening here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 106.953,
          "en": "Do you have an idea?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.81,
          "end": 112.22999999999999,
          "en": "The behavior here, as I just mentioned, is not a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 117.22999999999999,
          "en": "We load our data by using this snapshot object on the route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.75,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "Now if we load a new route, what happens?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "Angular has a look at our app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "finds the fitting route here, hopefully,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "loads the component, initializes the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "and gives us the data by accessing the snapshot here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "Now that only happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 139.38,
          "en": "if we haven't been on this component before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.38,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "But if we click this link which is on the user component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 146.16,
          "en": "well then, the URL still changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "but we already are on the component which should get loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 154.57999999999998,
          "en": "So Angular cleverly doesn't reinstantiate this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "That would only cost us performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 161.52,
          "en": "Why would it rerender a component we already are on?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.52,
          "end": 165,
          "en": "Now you might say, because the data we want to load changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "but Angular doesn't know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 168.42000000000002,
          "en": "And it's good that by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.42000000000002,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "it won't recreate the whole component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "and destroy the old one if we already are on that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 178.71,
          "en": "Still, of course you want to get access to the updated data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.71,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "And you can.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 185.19,
          "en": "It's fine to use the snapshot for the first initialization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 188.49,
          "en": "but to be able to react to subsequent changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 190.113,
          "en": "we need a different approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.95,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "In our typescript code and ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 196.44,
          "en": "here, let's say after we assign this initial setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.44,
          "end": 198.39,
          "en": "we can use our route object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.39,
          "end": 200.232,
          "en": "and instead of using the snapshot here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.232,
          "end": 205.232,
          "en": "there is some params property on this route object itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.29,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "Now we didn't use that before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "We had the snapshot in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 210.543,
          "en": "What's the difference?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.5,
          "end": 214.62,
          "en": "Params here is an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 217.14,
          "en": "and now observables is something I will come to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.14,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "right after the section where we will take a closer look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 224.76,
          "en": "Basically observables are a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.76,
          "end": 228.03,
          "en": "added by some other third party package, not by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.03,
          "end": 230.52,
          "en": "but heavily used by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 234.27,
          "en": "which allow you to easily work with asynchronous tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.27,
          "end": 236.67000000000002,
          "en": "And this is an asynchronous task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.67000000000002,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "because the parameters of your currently loaded route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 242.46,
          "en": "might change at some point in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 242.46,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "if the user clicks this link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 245.1,
          "en": "But you don't know when.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.1,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "You don't know if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "And you don't know how long it will take.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 251.46,
          "en": "So therefore you can't block your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.46,
          "end": 253.38,
          "en": "and wait for this to happen here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.38,
          "end": 255.6,
          "en": "because it might never happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.6,
          "end": 257.64,
          "en": "So an observable is an easy way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.64,
          "end": 260.1,
          "en": "to subscribe to some event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.1,
          "end": 262.56,
          "en": "which might happen in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.56,
          "end": 265.56,
          "en": "to then execute some code when it happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.56,
          "end": 267.84,
          "en": "without having to wait for it now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.84,
          "end": 269.28,
          "en": "And that is what params is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.28,
          "end": 270.63,
          "en": "It is such an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 272.97,
          "en": "and as the name implies, we can observe it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 272.97,
          "end": 276,
          "en": "and we do so by subscribing to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 278.61,
          "en": "So you can call the subscribe method on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 278.61,
          "end": 281.01,
          "en": "And this is still called on params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.01,
          "end": 282.956,
          "en": "I'm just bringing it in a new line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 282.956,
          "end": 285.3,
          "en": "to make it easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 285.3,
          "end": 289.59000000000003,
          "en": "And now subscribe can take free functions you pass here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.59000000000003,
          "end": 291.27,
          "en": "as arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.27,
          "end": 294.99,
          "en": "Now the first one is the most important one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 294.99,
          "end": 296.2,
          "en": "It will be fired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 296.2,
          "end": 301.2,
          "en": "whenever new data is sent fruited observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 301.26,
          "end": 302.73,
          "en": "So to put it in easier words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.73,
          "end": 305.64,
          "en": "whenever the parameters change in this use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 305.64,
          "end": 307.77,
          "en": "So then this first argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 307.77,
          "end": 310.02,
          "en": "which should be a function here, is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 310.02,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "I will use a ES6 arrow function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 317.43,
          "en": "and here we will get the updated params as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 317.43,
          "end": 319.65,
          "en": "And you can set this type of params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 319.65,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "doesn't really make a difference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.54,
          "en": "has to be imported from at Angular router than though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 324.54,
          "end": 326.94,
          "en": "But anyways, params will always be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 326.94,
          "end": 328.65,
          "en": "just like here on the snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 328.65,
          "end": 332.13,
          "en": "which holds the parameters you define in the route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 332.13,
          "end": 333.87,
          "en": "as properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 333.87,
          "end": 336.9,
          "en": "So in the function body of this arrow function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 336.9,
          "end": 338.73,
          "en": "so of this function, which gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 338.73,
          "end": 341.25,
          "en": "whenever the parameter changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 341.25,
          "end": 344.43,
          "en": "here we can now update our user object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 344.43,
          "end": 346.124,
          "en": "and we can say this user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 346.124,
          "end": 349.02,
          "en": "should now be params ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 349.02,
          "end": 351.21,
          "en": "referring to the params we passed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 354.123,
          "en": "And the same of course for the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 355.35,
          "end": 358.08,
          "en": "Oops, with a semicolon at the end, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 358.08,
          "end": 360.51,
          "en": "So this will now update our user object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 360.51,
          "end": 362.97,
          "en": "whenever the parameter change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 362.97,
          "end": 364.11,
          "en": "That's why it's inside of this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 364.11,
          "end": 366.48,
          "en": "call back end of this anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 366.48,
          "end": 368.64,
          "en": "past three subscribe method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 368.64,
          "end": 372.39,
          "en": "This code will not be executed when ngOnInit runs through.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 372.39,
          "end": 373.65,
          "en": "This code here will.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 373.65,
          "end": 375.51,
          "en": "So the subscription will be set up",
